schema: "0.4"
id: echo-of-manifestation-map-the-threshold
type: image
quality: medium

prompt:
  text: >
    Top-down dungeon map of The Threshold — Zone 8 (Final Zone) of Echo of Manifestation, a survival
    horror roguelite. Dark fantasy game design document style, bird's-eye architectural floor plan.

    This is the final zone map — reality and echo merge completely. The map itself should feel like it
    is dissolving at the edges. NO COLOR — only black, white, and gray tones. The map should feel
    like looking at a document that is being erased as you read it:

    ENTRY (south): "THE NARTHEX" — The antechamber to the final domain. Reality frays at the edges —
    room borders dissolve into static/noise texture at the periphery. Resonance density indicators
    shown as thick black static fills at the edges. Two essence nodes embedded in the last stable
    wall sections. Five shadow nodes: in the static-frayed edges, inside amalgam enemies, at the
    threshold of visibility. REALITY EROSION hazard shown as the arena contracting — edges drawn with
    dissolution texture and contraction arrows with a 30-second timer. Touching the void edge = instant
    death markers. Enemy amalgam icons drawn as fused shapes from all previous zone types.

    THE RESONANCE EQUATION — PUZZLE (west): 12m x 12m. A floating equation written in pure resonance
    shown as mathematical symbols on floating platforms over a void floor. The void beneath rendered
    as pure black. Symbol platforms drawn as white geometric shapes floating in darkness. One essence
    node at the equation's solution point. Three shadow nodes attached to incorrect platforms. VOID
    FALL hazard shown with drop indicators and 20% HP loss markers. Three-fail combat escalation
    indicator.

    THE FINAL ARMORY — LOOT (east): 16m x 10m. The last supply cache. Weapons and items from every
    zone line the walls — each weapon drawn with a small zone-icon indicating its origin. Five essence
    nodes distributed across weapon racks. Two shadow nodes disguised as high-tier items. ROOM COLLAPSE
    timer shown as a 60-second countdown with acceleration markers (each item taken = -5 seconds).
    A TIME DILATION POCKET behind the northern wall revealed only after taking at least 3 items.

    BETWEEN THE FRAMES — SECRET (accessible through a reality tear in The Narthex): 10m x 10m drawn
    with dashed border. A space outside of time — everything hangs suspended, drawn as frozen elements
    with motion lines stopped mid-action. The final boss arena visible through a translucent wall,
    shown as a ghosted preview of the boss room layout. Two essence nodes floating in frozen time.
    NO SHADOW NODES — marked as outside shadow's domain. TEMPORAL DRAG hazard shown as a 90-second
    timer with escalating damage indicators. This room allows scouting the final boss — a tactical
    advantage icon marked. Shortcut indicator bypassing the Resonance Equation.

    THE MANIFESTATION — BOSS (north): 26m x 26m final arena. THIS ROOM IS THE BOSS — walls, floor,
    and ceiling drawn as organic surfaces with eye/mouth patterns suggesting the room itself is alive.
    The space shifts geometry shown as multiple overlapping room outlines at different angles
    representing different phases. Five essence nodes at survival anchors keeping the arena stable —
    destroying them empowers the boss but reveals the TDP. Eight shadow nodes woven into arena
    geometry — each marked with a zone-specific icon and that zone's hazard property indicator.
    ARENA MUTATION cycle shown with phase transition indicators: walls close, floor opens, gravity
    reverses, previous zone hazard zones manifest at random. A TIME DILATION POCKET revealed at
    center only after all 5 essence nodes are destroyed. Boss marker: "THE MANIFEST" — no single
    creature icon, instead the room ITSELF is the boss designation. The entire arena border pulses
    with convergence lines showing all resonance in the game flowing into this space.

    CRISIS CHOICE POINT (beyond the boss): After defeating The Manifest, a split path marker showing
    three options:
    - LEFT PATH: "Free Echo/Amara — Risk Zone Escape" (Escape ending)
    - CENTER PATH: "Synthesis — Both Escape" (Synthesis ending)
    - RIGHT PATH: "Leave Her — Safe Exit" (Sacrifice ending)

    The entire map has dissolution edges — borders fade from solid black line into static noise into
    pure white void. All previous zone hazard icons recur at random positions. The map should feel
    like a document that is aware it is being read and is trying to resist being understood.

    Map legend: White diamond = Essence Node, Dark circle = Shadow Node, White circle = Time
    Dilation Pocket, Dashed border = Secret Room, Living-room icon = Boss (The Manifest),
    Dissolution edge = Reality Erosion, Zone hazard icons = Recurring Hazards.

    Style: Architectural blueprint on pure white background dissolving into pure black at the
    northern edge. Room walls only in black and white — no color whatsoever. The player IS the light
    source — lighting shown as a radial gradient emanating from the player's entry point. Shadows
    move independently shown as shadow shapes that don't match their casting objects. Self-illuminated
    quality. Professional game design document aesthetic pushed to its absolute limit — the map
    itself should feel like it exists at the boundary between documentation and the thing it
    documents. Minimalist, stark, oppressive.
  negative: "color, any color, warm tones, cool tones, sepia, cream, bright, cartoon, anime, 3D rendered, photorealistic, standard architecture, cheerful, detailed textures, low detail, gradient fills, anything other than black white and gray"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1536
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"

tags: [map, zone-8, the-threshold, top-down, dungeon-map, game-design-document, dark-fantasy, final-zone, black-and-white]
